# Alembic Migrations

Alembic manages all PostgreSQL schema changes for Vibe-HR backend.

## Setup

- Config: `backend/alembic.ini` (script_location = migrations)
- env.py: reads DATABASE_URL from `app.core.config.settings` (never hardcoded)
- Run all commands from the `backend/` directory

## Development Workflow

### Making a model change

1. Edit `app/models/entities.py` (or `app/models/tra.py`) to add/modify a column or table.
2. Generate a migration:
   ```
   cd backend
   ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe what changed"
   ```
3. Review the generated file in `migrations/versions/`. Confirm the `upgrade()` and
   `downgrade()` functions look correct. Never run an unreviewed migration in production.
4. Apply to local DB:
   ```
   ./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
   ```

### Checking for pending migrations

```
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic check
```

Exits 0 when the DB is up to date; exits 1 (and prints operations) when new changes
are detected. Run this in CI to catch missing migrations.

### Other useful commands

```
# Show current revision
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic current

# Show migration history
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic history --verbose

# Downgrade one step
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic downgrade -1

# Generate SQL for offline review (no DB connection needed)
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m alembic upgrade head --sql
```

## Tests

Tests in `backend/tests/` use SQLite in-memory with `SQLModel.metadata.create_all`.
They are intentionally decoupled from Alembic migrations, which target PostgreSQL only.
Do not change test fixtures to use Alembic.

## Drift detection

`backend/scripts/check_schema_drift.py` compares model metadata table/column
existence against `information_schema`. Run it to detect out-of-band schema changes:

```
./.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m scripts.check_schema_drift
```

Exits 0 when clean, 1 when structural drift is detected.

## Baseline (470095da5995)

The initial revision captures the full schema as of 2026-07-09.
`alembic stamp head` was applied to the existing `myhr` DB without running DDL.
Known myhr items that differ from the model (to be addressed in a follow-up revision):

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| extra table `users` | Legacy artifact; 0 rows, no FK refs; safe to drop |
| duplicate index `ux_auth_users_login_id` | Identical to `ix_auth_users_login_id`; safe to drop |
| `PAP_APPRAISAL_MASTERS` index name casing | DB has lowercase prefix (`ix_pap_appraisal_masters_*`); model produces uppercase (`ix_PAP_APPRAISAL_MASTERS_*`) |
| `tim_attendance_daily.calculated_at` type | DB has TIMESTAMPTZ; model declares timezone-naive datetime (init_db DO $$ bug) |
